## 23. Functional Acceptance Criteria

Do not consider the application complete until the following workflows work:

1. A user can log in to the demo environment and navigate between every page.
2. Dashboard figures update when underlying demo data changes.
3. Inventory search, filtering, sorting, pagination, and product details work.
4. Stock receipt updates inventory without duplicate quantity increments.
5. QR scanning or manual batch lookup opens the correct batch.
6. Sales checkout validates stock, applies pricing rules, and produces an invoice.
7. Expired products cannot be sold.
8. FEFO selects the earliest-expiring eligible batch.
9. Batch expiry alerts and low-stock alerts reflect the underlying data.
10. Product history displays recorded events in chronological order.
11. Blockchain operations clearly distinguish pending, committed, and failed states.
12. Reports can be filtered and exported.
13. Role restrictions are enforced by the backend.
14. Forms show useful validation and error messages.
15. All major layouts work on desktop, tablet, and mobile.
16. No buttons, links, filters, or navigation elements are merely decorative.
17. Demo mode works without Fabric credentials, while production mode uses the configured backend and Fabric network.
18. No successful blockchain transaction is fabricated when the network is unavailable.

